#: ../../../reference/accessibility/orca-preferences/index.md:0
msgid ""
"Reference for Orca preferences that customize screen reader behavior in all "
"applications, such as key echo, speech, Braille and voices."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/accessibility/orca-preferences/index.md:7
msgid "Topics: Accessibility"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/accessibility/orca-preferences/index.md:11
msgid "Screen reader preferences"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/accessibility/orca-preferences/index.md:13
msgid ""
"Orca preferences allow you to customize functionality in Orca which applies "
"to all applications. An example of an Orca preference is key echo because "
"key echo is something that applies to all applications."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/accessibility/orca-preferences/index.md:15
msgid ""
"Orca preferences can be configured globally or on the application level. "
"Application-level preferences allow you to customize Orca functionality that "
"only applies in certain environments, such as on web pages or in chat "
"applications. As a result, you will only find these options available in the "
"application-specific preferences dialogs and only for those applications to "
"which these options apply."
msgstr ""

